            <section id="avoiding-burnout" class="mb-12">
              <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Avoiding Burnout</h3>
                
                <div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
                  <p>
                    Nomad life can be exhilarating, but it's also exhausting. Constant travel can lead to:
                  </p>
                  
                  <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
                    <li>Decision fatigue</li>
                    <li>Disrupted sleep</li>
                    <li>Work-life imbalance</li>
                    <li>Emotional exhaustion</li>
                  </ul>
                  
                  <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Preventative Measures:</h4>
                  
                  <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
                    <li><strong>Slow Travel:</strong> Spend more time in each place (1–3 months minimum).</li>
                    <li><strong>Rest Periods:</strong> Take offline days, digital detox weekends, or full sabbaticals.</li>
                    <li><strong>Home Bases:</strong> Some nomads keep a storage unit, rent a permanent apartment part-time, or rotate between a few familiar locations.</li>
                    <li><strong>Community Care:</strong> Forming stable circles of support helps with emotional stability.</li>
                  </ul>
                  
                  <p>
                    Recognizing the signs early and acting on them can save nomads from burnout or abandoning the lifestyle entirely.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>

